<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <!-- ORCHESTRA_ROOT=__ROOT__
       Read by lib/cli/heartbeat.mjs's installedRoot() to recover which project's checkout this
       installed agent was rendered for — the check that lets `install-heartbeat` refuse to
       overwrite an agent belonging to a different root, and that lets `orchestra doctor` report an
       agent left behind by a checkout that no longer exists. Never edit this line by hand: it is
       rendered by `orchestra install-heartbeat`, once per checkout. -->

  <!-- This is a LaunchAgent, not a cron job. A crontab entry runs outside the user's login session
       and cannot read the login keychain, which is what `claude`'s own auth reads — on the night
       of 2026-08-12/13 in planetCraft every cron tick died on "Not logged in", eight consecutive
       ticks, seven hours frozen. A LaunchAgent runs inside the login session and sees the keychain.

       __ID__ is the six-hex hash of this project's absolute path (`projectId`, lib/paths.mjs) — the
       only thing that stays unique when two checkouts of one repository, or two unrelated projects
       sharing a directory name, each install a heartbeat.

       This file is a TEMPLATE: `__ROOT__`/`__ROOT_XML__` and `__ID__` are the only things in it
       that are not literal. launchd needs an absolute path and expands nothing, so one committed
       file could never name two developers' checkouts. `orchestra install-heartbeat` renders this
       into ~/Library/LaunchAgents with the paths of the checkout it is run from, on every run, so
       a moved checkout self-heals. The installed agent is therefore one substitution away from
       this file, and `orchestra doctor` re-renders it to check that it still is, rather than
       letting the real schedule live only in ~/Library/LaunchAgents where it can be neither
       reviewed nor recovered.

       TWO substitutions of the same root, never used in the other's place: `__ROOT__` (raw) in the
       marker comment above, `__ROOT_XML__` (XML-escaped — `&`→`&amp;`, `<`→`&lt;`, `>`→`&gt;`) in
       every `<string>` element below. A `<string>` element is parsed XML content, where `&`/`<`
       are not literal; an XML comment is not parsed for markup at all, so escaping the marker's
       copy would only make `installedRoot()` read back `&amp;` where the real root has `&`, which
       never compares equal to it — reproducing the exact "a project refuses itself" failure this
       marker exists to prevent. Put the raw form in a comment, the escaped form in element
       content, and never swap them. -->
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>com.orchestra.__ID__</string>

  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>__ROOT_XML__/.orchestra/tick.sh</string>
  </array>

  <!-- Hourly, on the :13, as a CALENDAR interval rather than StartInterval 3600. The difference is
       what happens across sleep: StartInterval simply stops counting, and eight slots of 1h23 to
       3h26 were lost that way in one 46-hour roadmap in planetCraft — about six hours, one of them
       killing a worker mid-turn. launchd fires a missed calendar slot when the machine wakes. -->
  <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
  <array>
    <dict><key>Minute</key><integer>13</integer></dict>
  </array>

  <!-- templates/tick.sh keeps its own lock (`orchestra lock`), so a slow tick cannot pile up on
       the next one. -->
  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <false/>

  <!-- Without this, launchd kills every remaining process in the job's process group the moment
       the tick exits (launchd.plist(5): "When a job dies, launchd kills any remaining processes
       with the same process group ID as the job"). Reparenting to PID 1 does not help — launchd
       kills by process group, not by parent.

       This job exists to leave things running behind it: the tick's `caffeinate` is meant to
       outlive it by ninety minutes, and any worker session the tick launches is meant to outlive
       it for however long that worker runs. Without AbandonProcessGroup both would die with the
       tick instead, collapsing the window to the duration of the tick itself — the one stretch the
       machine was never going to sleep through anyway. -->
  <key>AbandonProcessGroup</key>
  <true/>

  <!-- So tick.log can say who fired each tick: the agent (this plist sets ORCHESTRA_TRIGGER=agent)
       or a hand-run tick (ORCHESTRA_TRIGGER unset, which templates/tick.sh reads as "manual"). A
       log that cannot tell the two apart cannot answer the one question it exists to answer: did
       the heartbeat fire when it should have. Measured in planetCraft on 2026-08-14: fourteen tick
       lines could not answer whether the heartbeat survives sleep, because nothing recorded who
       fired each one. -->
  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>ORCHESTRA_TRIGGER</key>
    <string>agent</string>
  </dict>

  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>__ROOT_XML__/.orchestra/launchd.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>__ROOT_XML__/.orchestra/launchd.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
